    <bpmn:process id="W_W3585" name="W3585. Technology Strategy &amp; Multi-Year Technology Roadmap" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Business strategy cycle (links to VS-33.1); annual planning; major business/tech shift
Frequency: Annual + quarterly refresh
Volume: Enterprise technology roadmap
Owner: CIO / Chief Enterprise Architect
Participants: CIO, Chief Enterprise Architect, IT Leadership, Business Capability Owners, Strategy (links to VS-33), PMO (links to VS-112), Innovation (links to VS-30), Finance (links to VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W3585 — Technology Strategy &amp; Multi-Year Technology Roadmap</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3585_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3585_Lane1" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3585_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3585_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3585_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3585_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3585_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3585_Start3" name="Business strategy cycle (links to VS-33.1); annual planning; major business/tech shift">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3585_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3585_Task4" name="CIO/Chief Enterprise Architect translate business strategy into technology…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CIO/Chief Enterprise Architect translate business strategy into technology strategy: capability gaps and technology implications of BuildRight&#x27;s growth (200→300+ stores), ecommerce/marketplace expansion, omnichannel, net-zero/renewable (links to VS-108), and regulatory change (e-invoicing links to VS-79, data privacy links to VS-91); define the strategic technology outcomes
Responsible (R): CIO / Chief Enterprise Architect / Strategy
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3585_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3585_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3585_Task5" name="CIO/Chief Enterprise Architect build the multi-year technology roadmap…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CIO/Chief Enterprise Architect build the multi-year technology roadmap: initiatives by year (core-ERP evolution links to W3584, digital transformation links to W3587, portfolio rationalization links to W3577, technical-debt remediation links to W3578), dependencies/sequencing, resource/capacity (links to VS-19/VS-103), and the capex/OpEx envelope (links to VS-40/VS-33.1/VS-17.4)
Responsible (R): CIO / Chief Enterprise Architect / PMO / Finance
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3585_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3585_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3585_Task6" name="CIO ratify the technology roadmap with ExCo (links to VS-33.2/VS-36), align to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CIO ratify the technology roadmap with ExCo (links to VS-33.2/VS-36), align to the corporate plan and PMO portfolio (links to VS-112/W3545), communicate to the organization, and review/refresh quarterly against actuals (links to W3592) and change
Responsible (R): CIO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual + quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3585_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3585_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3585_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3585_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3585_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-570 (ensure controlled execution — Technology Strategy, Innovation Governance &amp; Architecture Analytics (PA-113.3).) | - operational: translation discipline; operational: quarterly refresh
Owner: CIO / Chief Enterprise Architect</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3585_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3585_Annotation8" targetRef="W3585_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
