    <bpmn:process id="W_W3586" name="W3586. Emerging Technology Evaluation &amp; Adoption Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Innovation pipeline (links to VS-30.1); technology radar (W3572); business need
Frequency: Per evaluation + quarterly radar
Volume: Emerging-technology candidates
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / Innovation
Participants: Chief Enterprise Architect, Innovation/Digital (links to VS-30), Enterprise Architects, Security (links to VS-27.3), Business Sponsors, PMO (links to VS-112), Procurement (links to VS-34)
Source: workflow W3586 — Emerging Technology Evaluation &amp; Adoption Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3586_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3586_Lane1" name="Innovation">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3586_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3586_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3586_Lane2" name="Chief Enterprise Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3586_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3586_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3586_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3586_Start4" name="Innovation pipeline (links to VS-30.1); technology radar (W3572); business need">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3586_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3586_Task5" name="Innovation/Chief Enterprise Architect scan and evaluate emerging technologies…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Innovation/Chief Enterprise Architect scan and evaluate emerging technologies relevant to BuildRight: AI/ML (links to VS-30.2), computer vision, IoT/sensors (links to VS-04 environmental monitoring), RPA/automation (links to VS-30.2), blockchain, edge computing, conversational/GenAI, and retail-specific tech (autonomous inventory, computer-vision shelf audit); assess maturity, fit, value, and risk
Responsible (R): Innovation / Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous + per evaluation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3586_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3586_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3586_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Innovation run POCs/pilots (links to VS-30.1) for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect/Innovation run POCs/pilots (links to VS-30.1) for promising candidates: business case, success criteria, architecture fit (W3570/W3580), security review (links to VS-27.3), and the decision to adopt/trial/hold/reject on the technology radar (W3572)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Innovation / PMO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per POC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3586_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3586_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3586_Task7" name="Chief Enterprise Architect govern adoption into the standard landscape: when a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chief Enterprise Architect govern adoption into the standard landscape: when a technology moves to adopt, update the ATL (W3572), reference architectures (W3570), and skills (W3574); sequence into the roadmap (W3585) and PMO (links to VS-112); retire failing experiments
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per adoption</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3586_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3586_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3586_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3586_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3586_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-144 (ensure architecture standards &amp; exception control.) | - operational: disciplined POC and radar model; operational: intake and ATL discipline
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / Innovation</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
