    <bpmn:process id="W_W3587" name="W3587. Architecture for Digital Transformation Programs" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Major transformation program (ERP evolution, omnichannel, AI, net-zero/digital, marketplace, store-format)
Frequency: Per program
Volume: Active transformation programs
Owner: Lead Solution Architect / Chief Enterprise Architect
Participants: Lead Solution Architect, Chief Enterprise Architect, Program Manager (links to VS-112/W3549), Business Sponsor, Innovation (links to VS-30), IT Operations (links to VS-27), Change Management (links to VS-30.3), Finance (links to VS-40)
Source: workflow W3587 — Architecture for Digital Transformation Programs</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3587_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3587_Lane1" name="Lead Solution Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3587_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3587_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3587_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3587_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3587_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3587_Start3" name="Major transformation program (ERP evolution, omnichannel, AI, net-zero/digital…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3587_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3587_Task4" name="Lead Solution Architect/Program establish the program architecture: target…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Lead Solution Architect/Program establish the program architecture: target architecture (business/data/application/technology/security), the gap from current state (W3577), transition architectures (phased), guiding principles (W3570), and the high-level roadmap; align to the program charter/business case (links to VS-112/W3551) and corporate strategy (links to VS-33)
Responsible (R): Lead Solution Architect / Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): Program Sponsor / CIO
Duration: Program initiation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3587_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3587_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3587_Task5" name="Lead Solution Architect govern architecture across the program&#x27;s component…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Lead Solution Architect govern architecture across the program&#x27;s component projects: solution-architecture review per project (W3580/W3571), cross-project consistency and dependency management (links to VS-112/W3550), integration architecture (W3579), data migration (W3581), and risk/technical-debt tracking (W3578); resolve architecture escalations
Responsible (R): Lead Solution Architect / Enterprise Architects
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Program life</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3587_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3587_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3587_Task6" name="Lead Solution Architect ensure transition to operations (links to VS-27.1) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Lead Solution Architect ensure transition to operations (links to VS-27.1) and ITAM (links to VS-99) at program closure (links to VS-112/W3560/W3561), validate benefits realization against the target architecture, and capture learnings into reference architectures (W3570) and maturity (W3576)
Responsible (R): Lead Solution Architect / PMO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Program closure</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3587_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3587_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3587_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3587_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
