    <bpmn:process id="W_W3588" name="W3588. Technology Investment Governance &amp; Architecture ROI" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Investment/business-case cycle (links to VS-112/W3551/W3588); budget cycle (links to VS-33.1)
Frequency: Per investment + annual
Volume: Enterprise technology investment portfolio
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / CFO
Participants: Chief Enterprise Architect, CFO/Finance (links to VS-17.4/VS-40), CIO, PMO (links to VS-112), Business Sponsors, Vendor Mgmt (links to VS-03/VS-34), BI (links to VS-28.1)
Source: workflow W3588 — Technology Investment Governance &amp; Architecture ROI</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3588_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3588_Lane1" name="Chief Enterprise Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3588_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3588_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3588_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3588_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3588_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3588_Start3" name="Investment/business-case cycle (links to VS-112/W3551/W3588); budget cycle (links to…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3588_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3588_Task4" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Finance define the technology investment governance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chief Enterprise Architect/Finance define the technology investment governance: TCO framework (license links to VS-99.2, infrastructure links to VS-27.2/W3582, integration links to W3579, operations links to VS-27.1, people links to VS-103, retirement links to W3578), business-case methodology (benefits, NPV/IRR/payback links to VS-40/W3551), and the approval authorities
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Finance
Accountable (A): CIO / CFO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3588_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3588_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3588_Task5" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Finance assess each technology investment: TCO…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect/Finance assess each technology investment: TCO, benefits/cost-avoidance (rationalization links to W3577, automation links to VS-30.2, risk reduction links to W3590), strategic alignment (W3585), architecture fit (W3571), and risk; recommend fund/defer/reject and feed prioritization (links to VS-112/W3547)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Finance
Accountable (A): CIO / CFO
Duration: Per investment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3588_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3588_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3588_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Finance track realized benefits and TCO vs. business…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chief Enterprise Architect/Finance track realized benefits and TCO vs. business case (links to VS-112/W3561/W3564), report technology-investment ROI and value to ExCo (links to VS-33.2) and governance (W3592), and feed learnings to future business cases
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Finance / BI
Accountable (A): CIO / CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3588_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3588_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3588_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3588_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3588_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-144 (ensure architecture standards &amp; exception control.) | - operational: TCO framework; operational: realized-benefit tracking (links to VS-112/W3561)
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / CFO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
