      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3589_Start3" name="Platform/vendor decision; contract renewal; portfolio change (W3577); strategy (W3585)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3589_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3589_Task4" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Vendor Mgmt define the platform and vendor strategy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chief Enterprise Architect/Vendor Mgmt define the platform and vendor strategy for enterprise systems: ERP, POS, WMS, ecommerce, MDM, BI, loyalty, payments, integration, cloud, security — the in-suite vs. build split under the two-tier doctrine, the consolidation/rationalization direction (links to W3577), and the strategic vendor portfolio
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Vendor Mgmt
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Strategy + per decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3589_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3589_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3589_Task5" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Vendor Mgmt/Procurement manage strategic…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect/Vendor Mgmt/Procurement manage strategic vendor/platform relationships and contracts: selection (links to VS-03/VS-34), TCO/commercial (links to W3588), SLA/performance (links to VS-67/W3562), lock-in/exit strategy, roadmap alignment (links to W3585), and security/third-party risk (links to VS-27.3); negotiate and renew
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Vendor Mgmt / Procurement / Legal
Accountable (A): CIO / CFO
Duration: Per contract + ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3589_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3589_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3589_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Vendor Mgmt govern vendor/platform changes via the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chief Enterprise Architect/Vendor Mgmt govern vendor/platform changes via the ARB (W3571) and ATL (W3572), monitor vendor health/roadmap/EOL (W3578), and manage multi-vendor/fallback strategy for critical platforms (links to VS-26/W3590); report to governance (W3592)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Vendor Mgmt
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3589_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3589_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3589_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3589_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
