    <bpmn:process id="W_W3590" name="W3590. Architecture Risk, Resilience &amp; Disaster-Recovery Design" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: EA strategy (W3569); new initiative; BCP cycle (links to VS-26); incident/near-miss
Frequency: Per initiative + annual BCP review
Volume: Enterprise architecture resilience
Owner: Enterprise Architects / BCP
Participants: Enterprise Architects, BCP/Resilience (links to VS-26), IT Operations (links to VS-27.1/VS-27.2), Security (links to VS-27.3), PMO (links to VS-112), Risk (links to VS-21.2)
Source: workflow W3590 — Architecture Risk, Resilience &amp; Disaster-Recovery Design</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3590_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3590_Lane1" name="Enterprise Architects">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3590_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3590_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3590_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3590_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3590_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3590_Start3" name="EA strategy (W3569); new initiative; BCP cycle (links to VS-26); incident/near-miss">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3590_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3590_Task4" name="Enterprise Architects/BCP define the architecture resilience and DR design…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Enterprise Architects/BCP define the architecture resilience and DR design standards: availability/recovery tiers (RTO/RPO per system criticality — POS Tier 1 links to VS-08, ERP, ecommerce links to VS-10), HA/DR patterns (W3582), single-points-of-failure elimination, regional/DR strategy, and POS offline resilience (model-company §15.3 / links to VS-08)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects / BCP
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Strategy + maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3590_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3590_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3590_Task5" name="Enterprise Architects/BCP design resilience into each initiative via the ARB…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enterprise Architects/BCP design resilience into each initiative via the ARB (W3571/W3580): availability/DR requirements, failure modes, chaos/failover testing, dependency resilience (W3579), data resilience (W3581), and security resilience (W3583); align to the BIA (links to VS-26.1)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects / BCP / IT Ops
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per initiative</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3590_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3590_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3590_Task6" name="Enterprise Architects/BCP validate resilience through DR exercises and failover…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enterprise Architects/BCP validate resilience through DR exercises and failover testing (links to VS-26.1/W3566), capture lessons into reference architectures (W3570), and feed architecture-risk to ERM (links to VS-21.2) and audit (links to VS-21); report resilience posture to governance (W3592)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects / BCP
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual + per exercise</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3590_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3590_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3590_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3590_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3590_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-144 (ensure architecture standards &amp; exception control.) | - operational: resilience design and dependency mapping; operational: failover/chaos testing
Owner: Enterprise Architects / BCP</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
