      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3591_Start3" name="EA strategy (W3569); ARB cycle; major change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3591_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3591_Task4" name="Chief Enterprise Architect map and engage EA stakeholders: ExCo/sponsor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chief Enterprise Architect map and engage EA stakeholders: ExCo/sponsor, business capability owners, project/program managers, IT operations/security/data, vendors, and audit/risk; define the engagement model and communication plan by audience
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3591_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3591_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3591_Task5" name="Chief Enterprise Architect communicate the EA strategy, roadmap (W3585)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect communicate the EA strategy, roadmap (W3585), standards (W3572), and decisions to the organization: architecture briefings, the ARB cadence (W3571), self-service repository (W3575), and change communications for major architecture shifts; business-language framing
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Enterprise Architects
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3591_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3591_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3591_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect gather stakeholder feedback on EA effectiveness…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chief Enterprise Architect gather stakeholder feedback on EA effectiveness (standards fit, ARB process, enablement), integrate to maturity/CI (W3576) and metrics (W3592), and adjust the engagement model; manage stakeholder issues and escalations
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3591_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3591_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3591_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3591_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3591_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-570 (ensure controlled execution — Technology Strategy, Innovation Governance &amp; Architecture Analytics (PA-113.3).) | - operational: business-language engagement and value demonstration; operational: enforcement gates and enablement
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
