        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W3592_Flow11_di" bpmnElement="W3592_Flow11"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W3592_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W3592_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W3592_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W3592_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1050" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W3592_Assoc9_di" bpmnElement="W3592_Assoc9"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5515" name="W5515. Sourcing Decision Gate Operation &amp; Capability Sourcing Register" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Capability sourcing proposal (new capability, replacement, renewal-with-change) or a registered re-evaluation trigger firing (e.g. &quot;ERP vendor ships native WMS at parity&quot;, &quot;260 stores&quot;)
Frequency: Monthly SIB + on demand; annual register reaffirmation at QBR
Volume: Every capability decision across the 188-VS estate routes through one gate — ~30–45 SIB assessments/year (new decisions, renewals-with-change, fired re-evaluation triggers) plus ~9 annual register reaffirmations
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (SIB assessment lead)
Participants: Head of Enterprise Architecture, SIB (CIO chair; affected IT PO/PM &amp; BPO; FinOps/TBM analyst links to VS-135; CFO delegate; SEC lead — TPRM links to VS-161; Head of Engineering for build cases; AAP Platform Lead for agentic decisions), Product Council (ratifies 3-year-TCO &gt; PHP 25M), CEO (in-suite-tier removal waiver, rare), ARB (links to W3571), vendor-portfolio analyst (Register secretariat), Procurement/Legal (links to VS-34/VS-100.3)
Source: workflow W5515 — Sourcing Decision Gate Operation &amp; Capability Sourcing Register</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5515_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5515_Lane1" name="Head of EA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5515_Lane2" name="ARB">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5515_Lane3" name="SIB">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5515_Lane4" name="Vendor-portfolio analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5515_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5515_Start6" name="Capability sourcing proposal (new capability, replacement, renewal-with-change) or a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5515_Task7" name="Head of EA run the scored use-EBS → build assessment with the affected PO/PM…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Head of EA run the scored use-EBS → build assessment with the affected PO/PM and BPO: strategic differentiation, EBS fit-to-standard gap, de-unification integration cost, data gravity, PH regulatory fit, 3-year TCO, talent/key-person risk, and exit strategy — ordered test in-EBS → build: if an EBS module ships the function (or can be configured to), the answer is use it; build is admitted only when the EBS-standard answer demonstrably does not exist
Responsible (R): Head of EA / Owning PO &amp; BPO
Accountable (A): CIO (SIB chair)
Duration: 6–10 hours/decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5515_Task8" name="Assemble the five mandatory appendices — no sourcing decision is valid without…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Assemble the five mandatory appendices — no sourcing decision is valid without them: IAP integration estimate (flows, contracts, latency budget, run cost — links to W3579); control-mapping appendix naming every touched control of the 808-control register with its post-change evidence source; FinOps-verified TCO sheet (links to W4100); run-cost &amp; talent plan for build decisions (the buy exit does not exist under the two-tier doctrine); re-evaluation trigger
Responsible (R): Head of EA / FinOps / SEC / IAP
Accountable (A): CIO (SIB chair)
Duration: Included in Step-1 pack</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5515_Task9" name="ARB record the architecture opinion (integration pattern, data ownership…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: ARB record the architecture opinion (integration pattern, data ownership, retirement of affected capabilities — links to W3571); SEC pre-read the TPRM tier and Philippine-localization posture for any sourcing proposal (links to VS-161)
Responsible (R): ARB / SEC
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: Per decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5515_Task10" name="SIB decide at the monthly board; vendor-portfolio analyst record the decision…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SIB decide at the monthly board; vendor-portfolio analyst record the decision in the Capability Sourcing Register — capability, value streams, posture, product/system, owning team, re-evaluation trigger — the single source of truth for what is sourced how
Responsible (R): SIB / Vendor-portfolio analyst
Accountable (A): CIO (SIB chair)
Duration: At monthly SIB</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5515_Task11" name="Route decisions exceeding SIB decision rights: 3-year TCO &gt; PHP 25M → Product…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Route decisions exceeding SIB decision rights: 3-year TCO &gt; PHP 25M → Product Council ratification; removal of a capability from the in-suite tier → CEO-noted waiver (rare; same weight as the v1.x single-vendor waiver)
Responsible (R): SIB / Product Council / CEO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per qualifying decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5515_Task12" name="Maintain the Register lifecycle: annual reaffirmation of every standing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Maintain the Register lifecycle: annual reaffirmation of every standing decision at QBR; re-evaluation triggers monitored (vendor roadmap, scale milestones, regulatory change); fired triggers re-enter the gate at Step 1; register feed to portfolio reporting (W3592) and the sourcing reserve/exit-reserve disclosure (links to VS-135)
Responsible (R): Vendor-portfolio analyst / Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5515_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5515_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5515_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5515_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-570 (ensure controlled execution — Technology Strategy, Innovation Governance &amp; Architecture Analytics (PA-113.3).) | - operational: no sourcing decision without the five mandatory appendices (IAP estimate, control-mapping, TCO, exit/run plan, re-evaluation trigger) | - operational: every capability decision recorded in the Capability Sourcing Register; in-suite-tier changes require a CEO-noted waiver
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (SIB assessment lead)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5515_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5515_Annotation14" targetRef="W5515_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
